 ## [0.39.1]
 
+`FixtureCell::try_new` returns typed `FixtureCellError` admission failures for
+trusted fixture images. All constructors use one setup path and verify the
+committed authority before opening the byte cell. Existing cell envelopes are
+admitted before Cell initialization; invalid history is refused without resetting
+the journal. Raw backing-memory operations and initial Cell publication retain
+their substrate panic behavior. This is an unbounded constructor; use the existing
+bounded constructors when the caller requires a byte ceiling before allocation.
+`into_memory` transfers the admitted virtual memory for explicit raw inspection
+without another bootstrap or hidden cleanup. Jobs qualification uses these
+contracts to preserve typed management refusals, corruption tests and frozen
+two-slot-image refusal; consumer adoption waits for reviewed publication.
+
 The optional `test-support` feature exposes `testing::FixtureCell` for explicit
 fixture byte cells. Callers choose the backing memory, owner, namespace, stable
 key and manager configuration; the helper retains the ordinary allocation runtime
